---
name: Cash sleeve
description: Spare cash above a £1,500 buffer parked in ERNS.L short-dated GBP bonds, sold back before any trade is blocked
type: feature
---
Idle cash earns nothing at the broker, so a deterministic cash sleeve parks anything above the working buffer in a cash-like fund.

- Fund: `ERNS.L` (iShares £ Ultrashort Bond, quotes in whole GBP ~101 — added to the GBX allowlist so it is never divided by 100).
- Buffer: £1,500 of cash always kept liquid; the sleeve is SOLD first whenever cash falls below it, so it can never block a trade.
- Sized by the cash balance only, never by a signal. Cash already committed to buys proposed earlier in the same tick is deducted before parking.
- Runs after the core-allocation block in `trading-engine.server.ts`; exempt from the concentration cap, target-weight nibbler and net-edge gate, like the core.
- Settings: `trading_controls.cash_sleeve_enabled / _symbol / _buffer`, surfaced on the Risk page. Reads fail safe to off.

Applies to every portfolio (live, live_sim, paper, backtest), not just the real book:
- Buffer scales with NAV: `min(max(configuredBuffer, 5% NAV), max(250, 25% NAV))`.
- Sleeve fund follows the book's base currency — GBP: configured `ERNS.L`; EUR: `XEON.DE` (Xtrackers EUR Overnight Rate). Other currencies keep cash as cash rather than importing FX risk.
